IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 9 GENERAL PROVISIONS: s 91 (the Minister's written order on acquisition of assets, business or equity interests of a telecommunication
-- licensee, designated business trust or designated trust) and s 92 (the separation order).
-- Seat: the relevant person acquiring the holding, and the telecommunication licensee (or trustee) that the order reaches.  The Minister's powers
-- are expressed as the conditions under which they may be used against that person.
-- 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 91 was s 69B, s 92 was s 69C.  Money figures are the fine ceilings the Act names.

§ `s 91 Power of Minister to issue written order relating to acquisition of assets, etc.`

-- src:6174 | 91.—(1) The Minister may issue a written order to any person that
-- src:6175 | acquires the assets or business of, or equity interests in, a
-- src:6177 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6178 | 125 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6180 | telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or designated
-- src:6181 | trust (called in this section the relevant person), that
-- src:6182 | telecommunication licensee, the trustee‑manager of that designated
-- src:6183 | business trust or the trustee of that designated trust (as the case may
-- src:6184 | be), or both the relevant person and that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6185 | trustee‑manager or trustee (as the case may be), if the Minister is
-- src:6186 | satisfied that —
-- src:6188 | (a) the relevant person is not a fit and proper person; and
-- src:6190 | (b) it is not in the national interest to allow the relevant person
-- src:6191 | to continue to own the assets or business of, or to hold the
-- src:6192 | equity interests in, that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6193 | designated business trust or designated trust (as the case
-- src:6194 | may be).
@ref s 91(1) (src:6174-6194)
GIVEN `the relevant person acquires the assets or business of, or equity interests in, a telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or designated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the relevant person is not a fit and proper person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is not in the national interest to allow the relevant person to continue to own the assets or business of, or hold the equity interests in, the licensee, trust or designated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(1): the Minister may issue a written order to the relevant person, to the licensee or trustee, or to both` MEANS
    `the relevant person acquires the assets or business of, or equity interests in, a telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or designated trust` AND `the Minister is satisfied that the relevant person is not a fit and proper person` AND `the Minister is satisfied that it is not in the national interest to allow the relevant person to continue to own the assets or business of, or hold the equity interests in, the licensee, trust or designated trust`

-- src:6198 | (2) The Minister may, in any written order issued under
-- src:6199 | subsection (1), direct the relevant person, that telecommunication
-- src:6200 | licensee, the trustee‑manager of that designated business trust or the
-- src:6201 | trustee of that designated trust (as the case may be), or both the
-- src:6202 | relevant person and that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6203 | trustee‑manager or trustee (as the case may be), to do all or any of
-- src:6204 | the following:
-- src:6206 | (a) direct the transfer or disposal of all of the assets, business
-- src:6207 | and equity interests acquired by the relevant person in that
-- src:6208 | telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or
-- src:6209 | designated trust (as the case may be) within such time and
-- src:6210 | subject to such conditions as the Minister considers
-- src:6211 | appropriate;
-- src:6213 | (b) restrict the transfer or disposal of the assets, business and
-- src:6214 | equity interests in that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6215 | designated business trust or designated trust (as the case
-- src:6216 | may be) by the relevant person;
-- src:6218 | (c) restrict the exercise of voting power in that
-- src:6219 | telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or
-- src:6220 | designated trust (as the case may be) by the relevant
-- src:6221 | person;
-- src:6223 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6224 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 126
-- src:6226 | (d) require that no payment be made by that
-- src:6227 | telecommunication licensee, the trustee‑manager of that
-- src:6228 | designated business trust or the trustee of that designated
-- src:6229 | trust (as the case may be) of any amount (whether by way
-- src:6230 | of dividends, profits, income or otherwise) in respect of the
-- src:6231 | equity interests acquired by the relevant person;
-- src:6233 | (e) restrict the issuance or offer of equity interests (whether by
-- src:6234 | way of rights, bonus or otherwise) by that
-- src:6235 | telecommunication licensee, the trustee‑manager of that
-- src:6236 | designated business trust or the trustee of that designated
-- src:6237 | trust (as the case may be) in respect of the equity interests
-- src:6238 | acquired by the relevant person.
@ref s 91(2) (src:6198-6238)
GIVEN direction IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(2): the Minister may include this direction in the written order` MEANS
    elem direction (LIST "the transfer or disposal of all of the assets, business and equity interests acquired by the relevant person, within such time and subject to such conditions as the Minister considers appropriate"
                       , "a restriction on the transfer or disposal of the assets, business and equity interests by the relevant person"
                       , "a restriction on the exercise of voting power by the relevant person"
                       , "a requirement that no payment be made of any amount, by way of dividends, profits, income or otherwise, in respect of the equity interests acquired by the relevant person"
                       , "a restriction on the issuance or offer of equity interests, by way of rights, bonus or otherwise, in respect of the equity interests acquired by the relevant person")

-- src:6242 | (3) In the case of any written order made under subsection (2)(a) or
-- src:6243 | (b) relating to the equity interests, until a transfer or disposal is
-- src:6244 | effected in accordance with the written order or until the restriction on
-- src:6245 | the transfer or disposal is removed (as the case may be), despite the
-- src:6246 | provisions of any written law or anything contained in the
-- src:6247 | memorandum or articles of association, trust deed or other
-- src:6248 | constitution, of that telecommunication licensee, designated
-- src:6249 | business trust or designated trust (as the case may be) —
-- src:6251 | (a) voting rights are not exercisable in respect of the equity
-- src:6252 | interests, unless the Minister expressly permits such rights
-- src:6253 | to be exercised;
-- src:6255 | (b) no equity interests of that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6256 | designated business trust or designated trust (as the case
-- src:6257 | may be) are to be issued or offered (whether by way of
-- src:6258 | rights, bonus or otherwise) in respect of the equity
-- src:6259 | interests, unless the Authority expressly permits such
-- src:6260 | issue or offer; and
-- src:6262 | (c) except in a liquidation of that telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6263 | designated business trust or designated trust (as the case
-- src:6264 | may be), no payment is to be made by that
-- src:6265 | telecommunication licensee, the trustee‑manager of that
-- src:6266 | designated business trust or the trustee of that designated
-- src:6267 | trust (as the case may be) of any amount (whether by way
-- src:6269 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6270 | 127 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6272 | of dividends, profits, income or otherwise) in respect of the
-- src:6273 | equity interests unless the Minister expressly authorises
-- src:6274 | such payment.
@ref s 91(3) (src:6242-6274)
GIVEN `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister expressly permits the voting rights to be exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(3)(a): the voting rights in respect of the equity interests are exercisable` MEANS
    (NOT `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests`) OR `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` OR `the Minister expressly permits the voting rights to be exercised`

GIVEN `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority expressly permits the issue or offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(3)(b): equity interests may be issued or offered in respect of the equity interests` MEANS
    (NOT `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests`) OR `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` OR `the Authority expressly permits the issue or offer`

GIVEN `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in a liquidation of the licensee, designated business trust or designated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister expressly authorises the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(3)(c): a payment may be made in respect of the equity interests` MEANS
    (NOT `the written order is made under subsection (2)(a) or (b) relating to the equity interests`) OR `the transfer or disposal has been effected, or the restriction removed` OR `the payment is made in a liquidation of the licensee, designated business trust or designated trust` OR `the Minister expressly authorises the payment`

-- src:6278 | (4) Before issuing the written order under subsection (1), the
-- src:6279 | Minister must, unless the Minister decides that it is not practicable or
-- src:6280 | desirable to do so, cause to be given to the relevant person and the
-- src:6281 | telecommunication licensee, designated business trust or designated
-- src:6282 | trust (as the case may be) written notice of the Minister’s intention to
-- src:6283 | issue the written order, specifying the date by which written
-- src:6284 | representations may be made to the Minister with regard to the
-- src:6285 | written order.
@ref s 91(4) (src:6278-6285)
GIVEN `the Minister decides that it is not practicable or desirable to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister caused written notice of the intention to issue the order to be given to the relevant person and the licensee, trust or designated trust, specifying the date by which written representations may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(4): the Minister may issue the written order under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the Minister decides that it is not practicable or desirable to give notice` OR `the Minister caused written notice of the intention to issue the order to be given to the relevant person and the licensee, trust or designated trust, specifying the date by which written representations may be made`

-- src:6289 | (5) Upon receipt of any written representation, the Minister must
-- src:6290 | consider it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the written
-- src:6291 | order.
@ref s 91(5) (src:6289-6291)
GIVEN `the Minister received a written representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considered it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(5): the Minister has acted as the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Minister received a written representation`) OR `the Minister considered it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the order`

-- src:6295 | (6) The Minister may vary or revoke any written order issued under
-- src:6296 | this section.
@ref s 91(6) (src:6295-6296)
GIVEN `the written order was issued under section 91` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(6): the Minister may vary or revoke the written order` MEANS
    `the written order was issued under section 91`

-- src:6300 | (7) Any person to whom a written order is issued under
-- src:6301 | subsection (1) must comply with the written order, and the written
-- src:6302 | order takes effect despite the provisions of any other written law and
-- src:6303 | anything contained in the memorandum or articles of association,
-- src:6304 | trust deed or other constitution, of the telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6305 | designated business trust or designated trust (as the case may be).
@ref s 91(7) (src:6300-6305)
GIVEN `the person was issued a written order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(7): the person must comply with the written order, which takes effect despite any other written law and the constitution of the licensee, trust or designated trust` MEANS
    `the person was issued a written order under subsection (1)`

-- src:6309 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (7) shall be guilty of an
-- src:6310 | offence and shall be liable on conviction —
-- src:6312 | (a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not exceeding
-- src:6313 | $125,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:6314 | 3 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence,
-- src:6315 | to a further fine not exceeding $12,500 for every day or
-- src:6316 | part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:6317 | conviction; or
-- src:6319 | (b) in any other case, to a fine not exceeding $250,000 and, in
-- src:6320 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:6322 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6323 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 128
-- src:6325 | exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:6326 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 91(8) (src:6309-6326)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 91(8): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be (the further daily fine is $12,500 for an individual, $25,000 otherwise)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the person contravenes subsection (7)` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the person is an individual` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 125000, 36, 12500, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE JUST (`Penalty` OF 250000, 0, 25000, FALSE)

-- src:6330 | (9) In this section —
-- src:6332 | “designated business trust” and “designated trust” have the
-- src:6333 | meanings given by section 37(1);
-- src:6335 | “equity interest” means —
-- src:6337 | (a) in relation to a telecommunication licensee, a voting
-- src:6338 | share in that telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6340 | (b) in relation to a designated business trust, a unit in that
-- src:6341 | designated business trust; or
-- src:6343 | (c) in relation to a designated trust, any right or interest,
-- src:6344 | whether legal or equitable, in that designated trust
-- src:6345 | which gives the holder of that right or interest voting
-- src:6346 | power in that designated trust.
@ref s 91(9) (src:6330-6346)
GIVEN `it has the meaning section 37(1) gives designated business trust or designated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(9): this is a "designated business trust" or "designated trust"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 37(1) gives designated business trust or designated trust`

GIVEN `it is a voting share in a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a unit in a designated business trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a right or interest, legal or equitable, in a designated trust which gives the holder voting power in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(9): this is an "equity interest"` MEANS
    `it is a voting share in a telecommunication licensee` OR `it is a unit in a designated business trust` OR `it is a right or interest, legal or equitable, in a designated trust which gives the holder voting power in it`

§ `s 92 Power of Minister to issue separation order`

-- src:6353 | 92.—(1) The Minister may issue a written order (called in this
-- src:6354 | section the separation order) to any telecommunication licensee
-- src:6355 | (called in this section the relevant telecommunication licensee), if —
-- src:6357 | (a) either of the following applies:
-- src:6359 | (i) the relevant telecommunication licensee is licensed
-- src:6360 | to operate a telecommunication system, or any
-- src:6361 | installation or plant used for telecommunications,
-- src:6362 | that is so costly or difficult to replicate that a
-- src:6363 | requirement to do so would create a significant
-- src:6364 | barrier to rapid and successful entry into the market
-- src:6365 | for telecommunication services in Singapore by an
-- src:6366 | efficient competitor of the relevant
-- src:6367 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6369 | (ii) the relevant telecommunication licensee has the
-- src:6370 | ability to exercise significant market power in any
-- src:6372 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6373 | 129 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6375 | market for telecommunication services in Singapore,
-- src:6376 | and both of the following apply:
-- src:6378 | (A) the telecommunication services provided by
-- src:6379 | the relevant telecommunication licensee in that
-- src:6380 | market (called in this subsection the relevant
-- src:6381 | telecommunication services) are required by
-- src:6382 | other telecommunication licensees for the
-- src:6383 | provision of telecommunication services in
-- src:6384 | Singapore on a competitive basis;
-- src:6386 | (B) it is so costly or difficult to provide the relevant
-- src:6387 | telecommunication services that a requirement
-- src:6388 | to do so would create a significant barrier to the
-- src:6389 | provision of telecommunication services in
-- src:6390 | Singapore on a competitive basis by an
-- src:6391 | efficient competitor of the relevant
-- src:6392 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6394 | (b) the Minister is satisfied that the actions that the Authority
-- src:6395 | has taken in the exercise of its powers under this Act have
-- src:6396 | failed, and that any other actions that the Authority may
-- src:6397 | take in the exercise of those powers are likely to fail, to
-- src:6398 | enable an efficient competitor of the relevant
-- src:6399 | telecommunication licensee to achieve —
-- src:6401 | (i) where paragraph (a)(i) applies, rapid and successful
-- src:6402 | entry into the market for telecommunication services
-- src:6403 | in Singapore; or
-- src:6405 | (ii) where paragraph (a)(ii) applies, the provision of
-- src:6406 | telecommunication services in Singapore on a
-- src:6407 | competitive basis; and
-- src:6409 | (c) the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to
-- src:6410 | issue the separation order.
@ref s 92(1) (src:6353-6410)
GIVEN `the licensee is licensed to operate a telecommunication system, or installation or plant used for telecommunications, so costly or difficult to replicate that a requirement to do so would create a significant barrier to rapid and successful entry into the market by an efficient competitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has the ability to exercise significant market power in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the services provided by the licensee in that market are required by other telecommunication licensees for providing telecommunication services in Singapore on a competitive basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is so costly or difficult to provide those services that a requirement to do so would create a significant barrier to the provision of telecommunication services on a competitive basis by an efficient competitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the actions that the Authority has taken have failed, and that any other actions it may take are likely to fail, to enable an efficient competitor to achieve rapid and successful entry, or the provision of telecommunication services on a competitive basis, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to issue the separation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(1): the Minister may issue a separation order to the relevant telecommunication licensee` MEANS
        (   `the licensee is licensed to operate a telecommunication system, or installation or plant used for telecommunications, so costly or difficult to replicate that a requirement to do so would create a significant barrier to rapid and successful entry into the market by an efficient competitor`
         OR (    `the licensee has the ability to exercise significant market power in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore`
             AND `the services provided by the licensee in that market are required by other telecommunication licensees for providing telecommunication services in Singapore on a competitive basis`
             AND `it is so costly or difficult to provide those services that a requirement to do so would create a significant barrier to the provision of telecommunication services on a competitive basis by an efficient competitor`))
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the actions that the Authority has taken have failed, and that any other actions it may take are likely to fail, to enable an efficient competitor to achieve rapid and successful entry, or the provision of telecommunication services on a competitive basis, as the case may be`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest to issue the separation order`

-- src:6414 | (2) In deciding whether it is in the public interest to issue the
-- src:6415 | separation order, the Minister must have regard to whether the issue
-- src:6416 | of the separation order is necessary or desirable for one or more of the
-- src:6417 | following purposes:
-- src:6419 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6420 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 130
-- src:6422 | (a) to promote and maintain fair and efficient market conduct
-- src:6423 | and effective competition between persons engaged in
-- src:6424 | commercial activities connected with telecommunication
-- src:6425 | systems and services in Singapore;
-- src:6427 | (b) to promote the efficiency and international
-- src:6428 | competitiveness of the telecommunication industry in
-- src:6429 | Singapore;
-- src:6431 | (c) to eliminate or reduce barriers to competition arising from
-- src:6432 | the control of any telecommunication system, or the
-- src:6433 | possession of significant market power, by the relevant
-- src:6434 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6436 | (d) to promote transparency, non-discrimination and
-- src:6437 | equivalence of supply in relation to the provision of
-- src:6438 | telecommunication services in Singapore.
@ref s 92(2) (src:6414-6438)
GIVEN purpose IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(2): the Minister must have regard to whether the separation order is necessary or desirable for this purpose` MEANS
    elem purpose (LIST "to promote and maintain fair and efficient market conduct and effective competition between persons engaged in commercial activities connected with telecommunication systems and services in Singapore"
                      , "to promote the efficiency and international competitiveness of the telecommunication industry in Singapore"
                      , "to eliminate or reduce barriers to competition arising from the control of a telecommunication system, or the possession of significant market power, by the relevant telecommunication licensee"
                      , "to promote transparency, non-discrimination and equivalence of supply in relation to the provision of telecommunication services in Singapore")

-- src:6442 | (3) The separation order may —
-- src:6444 | (a) direct the relevant telecommunication licensee to transfer
-- src:6445 | to a separate entity or an independent entity either or both
-- src:6446 | of the following:
-- src:6448 | (i) the whole or any part of any business of the relevant
