-- src:6495 | matters which, in the Minister’s opinion, are
-- src:6496 | necessary to ensure that the transfer directed under
-- src:6497 | paragraph (a) is effective.
@ref s 92(3) (src:6442-6497)
GIVEN direction IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(3): the separation order may contain this direction` MEANS
    elem direction (LIST "to transfer to a separate entity or an independent entity the whole or any part of any business conducted under a licence granted under section 5"
                       , "to transfer to a separate entity or an independent entity the whole or any part of any property used to provide telecommunication services, and any rights, obligations and liabilities relating to that property"
                       , "to establish a separate entity and ensure that it applies for a licence under section 5"
                       , "the types of transactions, dealings, arrangements and relationships the licensee may engage in, or is prohibited from engaging in, with the separate or independent entity"
                       , "the measures to be implemented to ensure that the licensee will not obtain effective control over the independent entity"
                       , "any future or contingent right or liability of the licensee"
                       , "the conditions of the transfer, including the payment of consideration by the transferee to the licensee"
                       , "any incidental, consequential or supplementary matters necessary to ensure that the transfer is effective")

-- src:6501 | (4) In determining the directions to be included in the separation
-- src:6502 | order, the Minister must have regard to whether the directions are
-- src:6503 | proportionate, taking into account —
-- src:6505 | (a) the contestability of the relevant market for
-- src:6506 | telecommunication services in Singapore; and
-- src:6508 | (b) the effectiveness of the directions in eliminating or
-- src:6509 | minimising any incentive or opportunity for the relevant
-- src:6510 | telecommunication licensee to act in a manner that
-- src:6511 | prevents, restricts or distorts competition in the relevant
-- src:6512 | market for telecommunication services in Singapore.
@ref s 92(4) (src:6501-6512)
GIVEN `the Minister has had regard to the contestability of the relevant market for telecommunication services in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has had regard to the effectiveness of the directions in eliminating or minimising any incentive or opportunity for the licensee to prevent, restrict or distort competition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(4): the Minister has determined the directions as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Minister has had regard to the contestability of the relevant market for telecommunication services in Singapore` AND `the Minister has had regard to the effectiveness of the directions in eliminating or minimising any incentive or opportunity for the licensee to prevent, restrict or distort competition`

-- src:6519 | (5) A licence granted under section 5 to a separate entity established
-- src:6520 | by a relevant telecommunication licensee may include (without
-- src:6521 | affecting the power to impose conditions conferred by that section)
-- src:6522 | conditions requiring the separate entity —
-- src:6524 | (a) to operate on a stand-alone basis;
-- src:6526 | (b) to deal at arm’s length with the relevant telecommunication
-- src:6527 | licensee or any of its associates;
-- src:6529 | (c) to provide to other telecommunication licensees any
-- src:6530 | service on the same terms and conditions (including in
-- src:6531 | relation to price, service levels and time frames), and by
-- src:6532 | means of the same systems and processes (including
-- src:6533 | operational support processes), as it provides to the
-- src:6534 | relevant telecommunication licensee or any of its
-- src:6535 | associates; and
-- src:6537 | (d) to do, or to refrain from doing, such things as are specified
-- src:6538 | in the licence, or as are of a description specified in the
-- src:6539 | licence.
@ref s 92(5) (src:6519-6539)
GIVEN condition IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(5): a licence granted under section 5 to the separate entity may include this condition` MEANS
    elem condition (LIST "to operate on a stand-alone basis"
                       , "to deal at arm's length with the relevant telecommunication licensee or any of its associates"
                       , "to provide to other telecommunication licensees any service on the same terms and conditions, and by means of the same systems and processes, as it provides to the relevant telecommunication licensee or any of its associates"
                       , "to do, or to refrain from doing, such things as are specified in the licence, or as are of a description specified in the licence")

-- src:6543 | (6) The separation order takes effect, despite —
-- src:6545 | (a) the provisions of any other written law or any rule of law;
-- src:6546 | and
-- src:6548 | (b) the provisions of the memorandum or articles of
-- src:6549 | association, trust deed, partnership agreement, limited
-- src:6550 | liability partnership agreement, or other constitution or
-- src:6551 | equivalent instrument, of the relevant telecommunication
-- src:6552 | licensee.
@ref s 92(6) (src:6543-6552)
GIVEN `the separation order was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(6): the separation order takes effect despite any other written law, rule of law, and the constitution of the relevant telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `the separation order was issued`

-- src:6556 | (7) Despite any other written law or any rule of law, where the
-- src:6557 | separation order contains a direction under subsection (3)(a), on the
-- src:6558 | date appointed for the transfer of any business or property of the
-- src:6559 | relevant telecommunication licensee to a transferee —
-- src:6561 | (a) that business or property is transferred to, and vests in, the
-- src:6562 | transferee without other or further assurance, act or deed,
-- src:6563 | and the separation order has effect according to its tenor
-- src:6564 | and be binding on any person thereby affected;
-- src:6566 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6567 | 133 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6569 | (b) every deed, bond, agreement or other arrangement
-- src:6570 | subsisting immediately before that date which relates to
-- src:6571 | that business or property, and to which the relevant
-- src:6572 | telecommunication licensee is a party, continues in full
-- src:6573 | force and effect, and is enforceable by or against the
-- src:6574 | transferee, from that date, as if the transferee had been
-- src:6575 | named in it or had been a party to it instead of the relevant
-- src:6576 | telecommunication licensee; and
-- src:6578 | (c) any proceedings or cause of action, by or against the
-- src:6579 | relevant telecommunication licensee, pending or existing
-- src:6580 | immediately before that date and relating to that business
-- src:6581 | or property, if continued, is enforceable by or against, the
-- src:6582 | transferee from that date.
@ref s 92(7) (src:6556-6582)
GIVEN `the separation order contains a direction under subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on or after the date appointed for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(7): the business or property is transferred to and vests in the transferee, and existing arrangements and proceedings are enforceable by or against the transferee` MEANS
    `the separation order contains a direction under subsection (3)(a)` AND `it is on or after the date appointed for the transfer`

-- src:6586 | (8) Subject to subsection (11), the Minister may award
-- src:6587 | compensation to the relevant telecommunication licensee for any
-- src:6588 | damage caused to it by reason of its compliance with the separation
-- src:6589 | order.
@ref s 92(8) (src:6586-6589)
GIVEN `the damage was caused to the relevant telecommunication licensee by reason of its compliance with the separation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no compensation is excluded by subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(8): the Minister may award compensation to the relevant telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `the damage was caused to the relevant telecommunication licensee by reason of its compliance with the separation order` AND `no compensation is excluded by subsection (11)`

-- src:6593 | (9) For the purposes of subsection (8), the Minister must, within
-- src:6594 | 6 months after the making of the separation order, by notification in
-- src:6595 | the Gazette, establish a scheme for determining the amount of any
-- src:6596 | compensation payable to the relevant telecommunication licensee.
@ref s 92(9) (src:6593-6596)
GIVEN `months after the making of the separation order that the Minister established, by notification in the Gazette, the scheme for determining the amount of compensation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(9): the Minister has established the scheme in time` MEANS
    `months after the making of the separation order that the Minister established, by notification in the Gazette, the scheme for determining the amount of compensation` AT MOST 6

-- src:6600 | (10) A scheme established under subsection (9) may provide for —
-- src:6602 | (a) the manner in which any compensation or consideration is
-- src:6603 | to be assessed, including methods of calculation, valuation
-- src:6604 | dates and matters to be taken into account or disregarded
-- src:6605 | when making valuations;
-- src:6607 | (b) the assessment to be made by an independent valuer
-- src:6608 | appointed by the Minister; and
-- src:6610 | (c) the remuneration and expenses of the independent valuer.
@ref s 92(10) (src:6600-6610)
GIVEN matter IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(10): the scheme may provide for this matter` MEANS
    elem matter (LIST "the manner in which any compensation or consideration is to be assessed, including methods of calculation, valuation dates and matters to be taken into account or disregarded when making valuations"
                     , "the assessment to be made by an independent valuer appointed by the Minister"
                     , "the remuneration and expenses of the independent valuer")

-- src:6614 | (11) No compensation is to be awarded under subsection (8) if,
-- src:6615 | when issuing the separation order, the Minister was satisfied that the
-- src:6616 | relevant telecommunication licensee had engaged in conduct that
-- src:6618 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6619 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 134
-- src:6621 | prevents, restricts or distorts competition in any market for
-- src:6622 | telecommunication services in Singapore, through —
-- src:6624 | (a) its control of the telecommunication system, or the
-- src:6625 | installation or plant used for telecommunications,
-- src:6626 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(i); or
-- src:6628 | (b) the exercise of its market power mentioned in
-- src:6629 | subsection (1)(a)(ii).
@ref s 92(11) (src:6614-6629)
GIVEN `when issuing the separation order the Minister was satisfied that the relevant telecommunication licensee had engaged in conduct that prevents, restricts or distorts competition in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore, through its control of the system, installation or plant mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `when issuing the separation order the Minister was satisfied that the licensee had engaged in such conduct through the exercise of its market power mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(11): compensation may be awarded under subsection (8)` MEANS
    NOT (`when issuing the separation order the Minister was satisfied that the relevant telecommunication licensee had engaged in conduct that prevents, restricts or distorts competition in a market for telecommunication services in Singapore, through its control of the system, installation or plant mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(i)` OR `when issuing the separation order the Minister was satisfied that the licensee had engaged in such conduct through the exercise of its market power mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(ii)`)

-- src:6633 | (12) Any compensation awarded by the Minister under
-- src:6634 | subsection (8) is to be charged on and paid out of the Consolidated
-- src:6635 | Fund.
@ref s 92(12) (src:6633-6635)
GIVEN `compensation was awarded by the Minister under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(12): the compensation is charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    `compensation was awarded by the Minister under subsection (8)`

-- src:6641 | (13) Before issuing the separation order, the Minister must, unless
-- src:6642 | the Minister decides that it is not practicable or desirable to do so,
-- src:6643 | cause to be given to the relevant telecommunication licensee written
-- src:6644 | notice of the Minister’s intention to issue the separation order,
-- src:6645 | specifying the date by which written representations may be made to
-- src:6646 | the Minister with regard to the separation order.
@ref s 92(13) (src:6641-6646)
GIVEN `the Minister decides that it is not practicable or desirable to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister caused written notice of the intention to issue the separation order to be given to the relevant telecommunication licensee, specifying the date by which written representations may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(13): the Minister may issue the separation order` MEANS
    `the Minister decides that it is not practicable or desirable to give notice` OR `the Minister caused written notice of the intention to issue the separation order to be given to the relevant telecommunication licensee, specifying the date by which written representations may be made`

-- src:6650 | (14) Upon receipt of any written representation, the Minister must
-- src:6651 | consider it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the
-- src:6652 | separation order.
@ref s 92(14) (src:6650-6652)
GIVEN `the Minister received a written representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considered it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the separation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(14): the Minister has acted as the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Minister received a written representation`) OR `the Minister considered it for the purpose of determining whether to issue the separation order`

-- src:6656 | (15) The Minister may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:6657 | whole or any part of the separation order.
@ref s 92(15) (src:6656-6657)
GIVEN `the separation order was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(15): the Minister may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the whole or any part of the separation order` MEANS
    `the separation order was issued`

-- src:6661 | (16) The relevant telecommunication licensee and any person
-- src:6662 | affected by the separation order must comply with the separation
-- src:6663 | order.
@ref s 92(16) (src:6661-6663)
GIVEN `the person is the relevant telecommunication licensee or is affected by the separation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(16): the person must comply with the separation order` MEANS
    `the person is the relevant telecommunication licensee or is affected by the separation order`

-- src:6667 | (17) Any person who contravenes subsection (16) shall be guilty of
-- src:6668 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction —
-- src:6670 | (a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not exceeding
-- src:6671 | $125,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:6672 | 3 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence,
-- src:6674 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6675 | 135 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6677 | to a further fine not exceeding $12,500 for every day or
-- src:6678 | part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:6679 | conviction;
-- src:6681 | (b) in the case of an entity which is granted a licence under
-- src:6682 | section 5, to a fine not exceeding the higher of the
-- src:6683 | following amounts:
-- src:6685 | (i) 10% of the annual turnover of that part of its business
-- src:6686 | in respect of which it is granted the licence, as
-- src:6687 | ascertained from its latest audited accounts; or
-- src:6689 | (ii) $1 million,
-- src:6691 | (b) and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:6692 | exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:6693 | which the offence continues after conviction; or
-- src:6695 | (c) in any other case, to a fine not exceeding $1 million and, in
-- src:6696 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:6697 | exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:6698 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 92(17) (src:6667-6698)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (16)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an entity which is granted a licence under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 92(17): the most the fine may be on conviction, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the person contravenes subsection (16)` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the person is an individual` THEN JUST 125000
           IF `the person is an entity which is granted a licence under section 5` THEN (IF (`annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1) GREATER THAN 1000000 THEN JUST (`annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1) ELSE JUST 1000000)
           OTHERWISE JUST 1000000

GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an entity which is granted a licence under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 92(17): the most the further fine may be for every day or part of a day of a continuing offence after conviction, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person is an individual` THEN 12500
           OTHERWISE 100000

-- src:6702 | (18) Subsections (4), (5)(a), (6), (7) and (8) of section 37 apply with
-- src:6703 | the necessary modifications to this section as they apply to Part 5A.
@ref s 92(18) (src:6702-6703)
GIVEN subsection IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(18): this subsection of section 37 applies with the necessary modifications to section 92` MEANS
    elem subsection (LIST "37(4)", "37(5)(a)", "37(6)", "37(7)", "37(8)")

-- src:6707 | (19) In this section —
-- src:6709 | “30% controller”, in relation to a telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6710 | means a person who, alone or together with the person’s
-- src:6711 | associates —
-- src:6713 | (a) holds 30% or more of the total number of voting
-- src:6714 | shares in the telecommunication licensee; or
-- src:6716 | (b) is in a position to control 30% or more of the voting
-- src:6717 | power in the telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6719 | “broadcasting licensee” has the meaning given by section 2(1)
-- src:6720 | of the Broadcasting Act 1994, but does not include a class
-- src:6721 | licensee as defined in section 2(1) of that Act;
-- src:6723 | “business” includes any business affairs, property, right,
-- src:6724 | obligation or liability;
-- src:6726 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6727 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 136
-- src:6729 | “consideration”, in relation to a transfer of any business or
-- src:6730 | property of a relevant telecommunication licensee, means the
-- src:6731 | payment of monetary or other consideration by the transferee
-- src:6732 | or any person on the transferee’s behalf to the relevant
-- src:6733 | telecommunication licensee for the transfer of the whole or
-- src:6734 | any part of the business or property of the relevant
-- src:6735 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6737 | [Act 13 of 2026 wef 02/10/2026]
-- src:6739 | “effective control”, in relation to a telecommunication licensee
-- src:6740 | or an independent entity, means the ability to cause the
-- src:6741 | telecommunication licensee or independent entity (as the
-- src:6742 | case may be) to take, or to refrain from taking, a major
-- src:6743 | decision regarding the management or operations of the
-- src:6744 | telecommunication licensee or independent entity (as the
-- src:6745 | case may be), and includes such control as may be exercised
-- src:6746 | over the telecommunication licensee or independent entity
-- src:6747 | (as the case may be) by a 30% controller of the
-- src:6748 | telecommunication licensee or independent entity (as the
-- src:6749 | case may be);
-- src:6751 | “independent entity” means an entity that —
-- src:6753 | (a) whether alone or together with its associates, does not
-- src:6754 | have effective control over any telecommunication
-- src:6755 | licensee or broadcasting licensee; and
-- src:6757 | (b) is not under the effective control of —
-- src:6759 | (i) any telecommunication licensee, whether alone
-- src:6760 | or with its associates; or
-- src:6762 | (ii) any broadcasting licensee, whether alone or
-- src:6763 | with its associates; or
-- src:6765 | (c) is not under the effective control of any other entity
-- src:6766 | which, whether alone or together with its associates,
-- src:6767 | has effective control over any telecommunication
-- src:6768 | licensee or broadcasting licensee;
-- src:6770 | “property” means assets of every kind, whether tangible or
-- src:6771 | intangible, movable or immovable, however acquired, and
-- src:6772 | includes —
-- src:6774 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6775 | 137 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:6777 | (a) any property, right or power of any description; and
-- src:6779 | (b) in relation to a telecommunication licensee, the
-- src:6780 | telecommunication licensee’s telecommunication
-- src:6781 | system and installation or plant used for
-- src:6782 | telecommunications;
-- src:6784 | “separate entity”, in relation to a telecommunication licensee,
-- src:6785 | means an entity which is a separate legal entity from the
-- src:6786 | telecommunication licensee, and includes any such entity the
-- src:6787 | equity interests of which are wholly owned by the
-- src:6788 | telecommunication licensee;
-- src:6790 | “significant market power” means the ability to unilaterally
-- src:6791 | restrict output, raise prices, reduce quality or otherwise act, to
-- src:6792 | a significant extent, independently of competitive market
-- src:6793 | forces;
-- src:6795 | “voting share” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the
-- src:6796 | Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 92(19) (src:6707-6796)
GIVEN `the person, alone or together with its associates, holds 30% or more of the total number of voting shares in the telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, alone or together with its associates, is in a position to control 30% or more of the voting power in the telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): the person is a "30% controller" of the telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `the person, alone or together with its associates, holds 30% or more of the total number of voting shares in the telecommunication licensee` OR `the person, alone or together with its associates, is in a position to control 30% or more of the voting power in the telecommunication licensee`

GIVEN `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994 gives broadcasting licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a class licensee as defined in section 2(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is a "broadcasting licensee"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994 gives broadcasting licensee` AND (NOT `it is a class licensee as defined in section 2(1) of that Act`)

GIVEN `it is a business affair, property, right, obligation or liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is within "business"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is a business affair, property, right, obligation or liability` THEN JUST TRUE OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `it is the payment of monetary or other consideration by the transferee, or a person on its behalf, to the relevant telecommunication licensee for the transfer of the whole or any part of its business or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is "consideration"` MEANS
    `it is the payment of monetary or other consideration by the transferee, or a person on its behalf, to the relevant telecommunication licensee for the transfer of the whole or any part of its business or property`

GIVEN `the person has the ability to cause the telecommunication licensee or independent entity to take, or to refrain from taking, a major decision regarding its management or operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a 30% controller of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): the person has "effective control" over the telecommunication licensee or independent entity` MEANS
    `the person has the ability to cause the telecommunication licensee or independent entity to take, or to refrain from taking, a major decision regarding its management or operations` OR `the person is a 30% controller of it`

GIVEN `the entity, alone or with its associates, has effective control over a telecommunication licensee or broadcasting licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is under the effective control of a telecommunication licensee or a broadcasting licensee, alone or with its associates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is under the effective control of another entity which, alone or with its associates, has effective control over a telecommunication licensee or broadcasting licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is an "independent entity"` MEANS
    (NOT `the entity, alone or with its associates, has effective control over a telecommunication licensee or broadcasting licensee`) AND (NOT `the entity is under the effective control of a telecommunication licensee or a broadcasting licensee, alone or with its associates`) AND (NOT `the entity is under the effective control of another entity which, alone or with its associates, has effective control over a telecommunication licensee or broadcasting licensee`)

GIVEN `it is an asset of every kind, tangible or intangible, movable or immovable, however acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is within "property"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is an asset of every kind, tangible or intangible, movable or immovable, however acquired` THEN JUST TRUE OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `it is a separate legal entity from the telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is a "separate entity"` MEANS
    `it is a separate legal entity from the telecommunication licensee`

GIVEN `the person has the ability to unilaterally restrict output, raise prices, reduce quality or otherwise act, to a significant extent, independently of competitive market forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): the person has "significant market power"` MEANS
    `the person has the ability to unilaterally restrict output, raise prices, reduce quality or otherwise act, to a significant extent, independently of competitive market forces`

GIVEN `it has the meaning section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 gives voting share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(19): this is a "voting share"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 gives voting share`

-- src:6802 | (20) A reference in this section to the issuing of a separation order
-- src:6803 | includes a varying of that order.
@ref s 92(20) (src:6802-6803)
GIVEN `the order is varied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(20): the reference to the issuing of a separation order includes the varying` MEANS
    `the order is varied`
